#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# polya_count

#% text
# `polya_count(G, k), (G, [w1, ...])`: the number of colourings with k colours up to the group, or the pattern inventory

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The number of colourings of the points with k colours up to the group is the cycle index at x(i) = k (Polya's theorem); with weights it is the pattern inventory, the cycle index at x(i) = sum of w_j^i.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
polya_count(cyclic_group(6), 2)
#% output
#= 14

#% cell
polya_count(dihedral_group(6), 2)
#% output
#= 13

#% cell
polya_count(cyclic_group(4), [r, b])
#% output
#= b*r^3 + r*b^3 + 2*b^2*r^2 + b^4 + r^4

#% section
# See also

#% text
